# Spring Boot 3 & Java 21 Rules

## Java 21 Conventions
- Use `record` for DTOs and immutable request/response data carriers.
- Use pattern matching for `switch` and `instanceof`.
- Use text blocks `"""..."""` for multi-line SQL or JSON.
- Virtual threads (Loom) are enabled in Spring Boot 3.3.

## Concurrency & SQL Rules (Inventory Service)
- Stock reservation MUST use atomic conditional SQL updates to prevent race conditions:
  ```sql
  UPDATE stock_levels 
  SET reserved = reserved + :qty, version = version + 1, updated_at = NOW()
  WHERE warehouse_id = :warehouseId 
    AND product_id = :productId 
    AND (on_hand - reserved) >= :qty;
  ```
- Do not compute stock balance in memory and save.
- Run `InventoryConcurrencyTest.java` (50 threads) if touching stock calculation.

## Error Handling & RFC 7807
- All REST controllers must return RFC 7807 `ProblemDetail` on errors:
  - `status`: HTTP status code
  - `title`: Short error name
  - `detail`: Detailed message
  - `instance`: URI of the request
- Global exception handlers extend `ResponseEntityExceptionHandler` or use `@ExceptionHandler(ProblemDetail.class)`.

## Database Migrations
- Use Flyway scripts in `src/main/resources/db/migration/`.
- Naming convention: `V{N}__{description}.sql`. Never modify existing applied migrations.
